    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "HWP The Property Specialists are delighted to present 129 New Row Square, The Liberties, Dublin 8 to the market. This two-bedroom, one-bathroom ground-floor apartment benefits from its own private entrance and offers an excellent opportunity for purchasers seeking a property in one of Dublin's most central and vibrant neighbourhoods.\n\nThe accommodation comprises two bedrooms, a bathroom and kitchen / living accommodation, all conveniently arranged at ground-floor level. The own-door access is a particularly attractive feature, providing the property with a greater sense of privacy and independence than a traditional apartment layout.\n\nThe property is being sold as seen and is in need of refurbishment and modernisation throughout, presenting an ideal opportunity for a purchaser to renovate and put their own stamp on the property. With the right investment, No. 129 offers excellent potential to create a comfortable city home in a highly convenient Dublin 8 location.\n\nNew Row Square is situated in the heart of The Liberties, one of Dublin's most historic and increasingly sought-after areas. The property enjoys the benefit of city living with an extensive range of shops, cafés, restaurants, pubs and everyday amenities all within easy reach.\n\nSome of Dublin's best-known attractions and amenities are close by, including The Guinness Storehouse, Teeling Whiskey Distillery, St Patrick's Cathedral, Christchurch Cathedral and Dublin Castle, while the city centre, Temple Bar and Grafton Street are all readily accessible.\n\nThe area is particularly well served by public transport, with numerous Dublin Bus services operating nearby and the Luas Red Line within easy reach. The property's central location also means many of the city's principal employment, education and leisure destinations can be reached on foot or by bicycle.\n\nThe property is convenient to Trinity College Dublin, TU Dublin's Grangegorman campus and several of Dublin's major hospitals, while the nearby Meath Street, Thomas Street and Francis Street areas provide an excellent selection of independent shops, cafés and local services.\n\nPlease note that the property is being sold as seen and requires refurbishment and modernisation. \n\nViewing is highly recommended."
      },
      {
